      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Terryville sits in that practical, easy‑to‑miss part of Suffolk County where the landscape feels lived in rather than packaged.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://wiki-cafe.win/index.php/Terryville,_NY_Essentials:_Historic_Development,_Scenic_Stops,_and_Local_Experiences_to_Try",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Terryville’s history and everyday landscape tell a story of a community shaped less by spectacle than by steady development.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://wiki-cafe.win/index.php/Terryville,_NY_Essentials:_Historic_Development,_Scenic_Stops,_and_Local_Experiences_to_Try",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Much of Terryville’s present‑day development reflects the suburban expansion that occurred across central and eastern Long Island after World War II.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.longislandguide.com/visit/terryville/",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Terryville is entirely unincorporated, meaning it does not have a separate village government.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.longislandguide.com/visit/terryville/",
